# eBay live quantity (do not regress)

Proven on production (`16259141` + `35852a4f`): Seller Hub qty no longer snaps back immediately. **Do not undo this.** Two-way qty is the product: INW qty save updates View Item; a Seller Hub qty revise becomes View Item after **one** 5-minute cron GetItem.

Inventory-API listings: View Item is `offer.availableQuantity`. Seller Hub/Trading qty does not update that offer by itself. Writes stay Inventory `bulk_update_price_quantity` in `apps/main/src/lib/channels/ebay/quantity.ts`.

## Must stay true

- `ebayCronShouldPushOutbound` is **error-retry only**. Never restore the `inwUpdatedAt > lastPushedAt && inwUpdatedAt > lastInboundAt` heuristic (shipping attach and other GetItem side effects bump `updatedAt` and snap INW qty onto the offer).
- After `resolvePassthroughChanges`, `changed.quantity` is false unless `ebayContentPushShouldWriteVariantQuantities` is true. Title/price/shipping must not PUT INW qty because live eBay ≠ INW.
- Catch-up (`chooseEbayLiveListingQuantity`) writes the offer **only when the chosen qty is not INW’s number**. Keep `inwPushedRecently`. Keep `opts.source === "webhook"` skip.
- ItemRevised stays ignored / disabled. Do not add `ReviseFixedPriceItem` for qty. Do not un-migrate Inventory listings.
- Do not copy listing-level GetItem `Quantity` onto a variation matrix (`ebayGetItemShouldApplyListingQuantity` stays false for per-option). Do not weaken `shouldBlockOutboundQtyOverwrite` in `sync-inventory.ts`.
- **Do not copy lagged GetItem variation Quantity onto `offer.availableQuantity`.** Reverted `54ed7187`: GetItem SKU qty lags after an INW/Hub edit; writing it onto the live offer made qty edits not stick. Catch-up must not treat “we read SKU rows” as a reason to overlay Trading onto the offer.

## If Hub vs View Item splits again

Dump `_tmp-ebay-qty-surfaces.ts` / `_tmp-ebay-simple-listing.ts`, then **stop**. Do not stack another qty patch in the same session.
